.TH @PROG@ 1 "@PROJECT_YEAR@" "@PROJECT_VERSION@" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
@PROG@, @COLON@ \- remove files using colon-path
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B @COLON@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
.I FILE
\&...
.br
.B @PROG@
.RI [ OPTION ]...
\&...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B @PROG@
is a colon-path aware wrapper around
.BR rm (1).
By default (when
.B COLON_WRAP
is unset), a built-in rewrite implementation rewrites path arguments and
removes files, then prunes empty parent directories along
.IR LEAF .
Set
.B COLON_WRAP=1
to invoke
.B rm
from
.B PATH
instead.
.PP
Each
.B BASE:LEAF
argument is rewritten to the physical path
.B BASE/LEAF .
After a colon-path file (or tree) is removed, empty parent directories along
.I LEAF
are removed with
.BR rmdir (2)
when possible.
.B BASE
itself is never removed.
.PP
See
.BR colon-path (7).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B @COLON@ .:d/e/f
Removes file
.BR d/e/f ,
then tries
.B rmdir d/e
and
.B rmdir d
if those directories are empty.
.TP
.B @COLON@ \-rf a/b:c/d
Runs
.B rm \-rf a/b/c/d ,
then prunes empty parents under
.B a/b
along
.BR c/d .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show wrapper help and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-colon\-dry\-run
Print the planned
.B rm
and parent
.B rmdir
steps without executing them.
When using the built-in rewrite (default), output is prefixed with
.BR (rewrite) .
.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-force
Ignore nonexistent files, never prompt.
.TP
.B \-i
Prompt before every removal.
.TP
.B \-I
Prompt once before removing more than three files, or when removing
recursively.
.TP
.B \-\-interactive[=WHEN]
Prompt according to WHEN: never, once
.BR (-I) ,
or always
.BR (-i) ;
without WHEN, prompt always.
.TP
.BR \-r ", " \-R ", " \-\-recursive
Remove directories and their contents recursively.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dir
Remove empty directories (like rmdir).
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Explain what is being done.
.TP
.B \-\-one\-file\-system
When removing recursively, skip mount points.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-preserve\-root
Do not treat
.B /
specially.
.TP
.B \-\-preserve\-root[=all]
Do not remove
.B /
(default).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B COLON_WRAP
When unset (default), use the built-in rewrite implementation.
When set to
.BR 1 ,
exec the stem of
.B $0
from
.B PATH
(\fBcolon-rm\fR → \fBrm\fR).
When set to a program name, exec that program instead.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rm (1),
.BR colon-rmdir (1),
.BR colon-path (7)
.SH AUTHOR
Written by @PROJECT_AUTHOR@ <@PROJECT_EMAIL@>.
